# Build context for BOTH images is the repo root (board-api via
# deploy/board-api/Dockerfile, board-web via ./Dockerfile), so the ignore rules
# live here rather than beside either package.
#
# Patterns are anchored at the context root and `*` does not cross a `/`, so a
# per-package directory needs the `**/` prefix to match at all.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
# ...except the one tracked env file that is build INPUT rather than a local
# secret. `vite build` runs in production mode, so it reads
# board-frontend/.env.production. That file holds only a comment today and the
# SPA reads only one VITE_ key anywhere (VITE_AUTO_REFRESH_MS), so excluding it
# costs nothing right now — the exception is here so a key added to it later
# reaches the build instead of vanishing from the context with no error.
!board-frontend/.env.production
**/*.log
**/coverage
**/.vitest
.git
